\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 From steppe to stable
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
The horses we know and love came from a different source. They emerged more than a thousand years later, about 4,200 years ago, in the Pontic-Caspian steppes of what is now southern Russia, the same region that gave rise to famous horse-riding warriors li
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 ke the Cossacks, the Golden Horde, and the Huns.
