\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Horses for courses
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Over time, humans developed distinct horse breeds with a wide range of phenotypes, from the tiny Argentinian Falabella, barely reaching a meter tall at the shoulder, to the towering French Percheron, capable of hauling tons; from horses with the standard 
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 gaits (walk, trot, canter, and gallop) to horses able to perform alternative gaits, like ambling, with no bounce, making them more comfortable to ride. The Icelandic horse\hich\f31506 \rquote \loch\f31506 
